#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[[quarkus-maven-plugin-goal-build-appartifact]]`link:#quarkus-maven-plugin-goal-build-appartifact[appArtifact]`\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"Coordinates of the Maven artifact containing the original Java application to build the native image for. If not provided, the current project is assumed to be the original Java application. The coordinates are expected to be expressed in the following format: groupId:artifactId:classifier:type:version With the classifier, type and version being optional. If the type is missing, the artifact is assumed to be of type JAR. If the version is missing, the artifact is going to be looked up among the project dependencies using the provided coordinates. However, if the expression consists of only three parts, it is assumed to be groupId:artifactId:version. If the expression consists of only four parts, it is assumed to be groupId:artifactId:classifier:type.\n"
"--"
msgstr "`link:#quarkus-maven-plugin-goal-build-appartifact[appArtifact]`"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "[[quarkus-maven-plugin-goal-build-appartifact]]`link:#quarkus-maven-plugin-goal-build-appartifact[appArtifact]`"
msgstr "`link:#quarkus-maven-plugin-goal-build-appartifact[appArtifact]`"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "Coordinates of the Maven artifact containing the original Java application to build the native image for. If not provided, the current project is assumed to be the original Java application. The coordinates are expected to be expressed in the following format: groupId:artifactId:classifier:type:version With the classifier, type and version being optional. If the type is missing, the artifact is assumed to be of type JAR. If the version is missing, the artifact is going to be looked up among the project dependencies using the provided coordinates. However, if the expression consists of only three parts, it is assumed to be groupId:artifactId:version. If the expression consists of only four parts, it is assumed to be groupId:artifactId:classifier:type."
msgstr "Coordenadas del artefacto de Maven que contiene la aplicación Java original a partir de la cual se va a compilar la imagen nativa. Si no se especifican, se da por hecho que el proyecto actual es la aplicación Java original. Las coordenadas deben expresarse en el siguiente formato: groupId:artifactId:classifier:type:version, siendo opcionales el clasificador, el tipo y la versión. Si falta el tipo, se supone que el artefacto es de tipo JAR. Si falta la versión, el artefacto se buscará entre las dependencias del proyecto utilizando las coordenadas proporcionadas. No obstante, si la expresión consta únicamente de tres partes, se supone que es groupId:artifactId:version. Si la expresión consta únicamente de cuatro partes, se supone que es groupId:artifactId:classifier:type."

